OpenBoot 4.23.0, as released by Sun Microsystems, Inc., and UltraViolet's
additions to it.

The OpenBoot source in this folder is Sun Microsystems' release of OpenBoot
4.23.0 (2006). Each of its files that carries a licence carries Sun's,
below; the files of the release that carry only a copyright notice and
"Use is subject to license terms" are part of the same release and are
distributed under the same terms. Some files are also Copyright Bradley
Forthware or FirmWorks (Mitch Bradley), whose Forth system OpenBoot is
built on, as their notices say. All but one of the files that carry only
"Use is subject to license terms" are among them (the Forth kernel,
library and meta-compiler in obp/fm, the SPARC assembler and
disassembler, the generic PCI probe, parts of obp/os and obp/pkg, and the
tokenizer's dictionary). FirmWorks released its own Open Firmware, which
comes from the same code, in 2006 with its files under the MIT licence,
also given below; most of these files, or their code, are in that release.

UltraViolet's additions and changes (the host build in host/, build.sh,
and the files that say so) are Copyright (C) 2026 Andy Taylor and are
distributed under the same terms as the release, below.

